, 157 long lines, 10 undocumented heartbeat scopes, and one goal-changing `show` have all been resolved. The tensor-inverse statements and proofs are unchanged; a fresh-context review found no API or semantic regression, and its stale-prose findings were reconciled. LSP reports zero diagnostics, and direct kernel elaboration passes with zero warnings in 3:22.73 at 8,260,368 KiB. Commits: `b85046f44`, `dea2b7c2f`. Keep this issue open for the remaining project-wide warning classes and final full-build recount."},{"id":"C-0003","item":"I-0319","author":"horizon","at":"2026-07-24T20:48:47.610232+00:00","provenance":{"run":"0046","session":"0042-horizon-ajc-optimize","role":"horizon","round":"2","rounds":"8","task":"ajc-optimize","task_title":"Make the project clean and optimized","projects":"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"},"body":"Clean-build recount complete: `lake build` passes all 8,727 jobs with 1,174 warnings across 51 project files, down exactly 285 from the inherited 1,459-warning baseline. `TensorObjInverse.lean` contributes zero warnings and built in the clean graph in 296s. Remaining warning concentration is led by `TensorObjSubstrate.lean` (350), `SectionGradedRing.lean` (174), and `QuotScheme.lean` (85); dominant classes are 716 long lines, 108 show-style warnings, 98 unused simp arguments, and 58 undocumented heartbeat scopes. Keep this item open. The total 2:16:31 wall time is not a valid regression benchmark because a stale 10 GiB LSP worker contended for the first 44 minutes and the shared host stayed heavily loaded; nevertheless `CechSectionContractibility` at 1,473s is the next clear elaboration hotspot."},{"id":"C-0004","item":"I-0319","author":"horizon","at":"2026-07-24T22:00:23.097494+00:00","provenance":{"run":"0046","session":"0044-horizon-ajc-optimize","role":"horizon","round":"3","rounds":"8","task":"ajc-optimize","task_title":"Make the project clean and optimized","projects":"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"},"body":"`TensorObjSubstrate.lean` is now directly warning-free. Its tensor, dual, restriction, and pullback declarations are unchanged; the pass only wraps terms and replaces development journals with stable mathematical explanations. The prior 350 line-length diagnostics are gone, exact target style replay reports zero errors, and `lake env lean AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/TensorObjSubstrate.lean` passes silently in 5:22.96 at 8,022,244 KiB. Commit: `98353cd99`. The 1,174-warning full-build baseline remains the last verified global count."},{"id":"C-0005","item":"I-0319","author":"horizon","at":"2026-07-24T22:04:37.272203+00:00","provenance":{"run":"0046","session":"0044-horizon-ajc-optimize","role":"horizon","round":"3","rounds":"8","task":"ajc-optimize","task_title":"Make the project clean and optimized","projects":"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"},"body":"A whole-project lake exe lint-style replay is not a file-scoped verifier: it reports 650 pre-existing Unicode/spacing findings and the absence of a local scripts/nolints-style.txt. Filtering that output to the exact AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/TensorObjSubstrate.lean path yields zero findings."},{"id":"C-0006","item":"I-0319","author":"horizon","at":"2026-07-24T22:42:17.344897+00:00","provenance":{"run":"0046","session":"0046-horizon-ajc-optimize","role":"horizon","round":"4","rounds":"8","task":"ajc-optimize","task_title":"Make the project clean and optimized","projects":"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"},"body":"`SectionGradedRing.lean` and `QuotScheme.lean` are now directly warning-free. SectionGradedRing removes 174 diagnostics and passes LSP plus direct kernel elaboration silently. QuotScheme removes its 85-warning baseline through current sheaf constructors, exact proof-style repairs, line wrapping, and heartbeat documentation; direct elaboration passes silently in 6:42.06 at 9,112,376 KiB. Commits: `e142308c0`, `fb29d460b`. Keep the issue open for the clean global recount."}]}
