{"id":"I-0313","status":"open","kind":"memory","body":"Lean --profile output order does not localize async kernel time

In Lean 4.31, `Elab.async` defaults to true and `Lean.addDecl` queues each kernel check asynchronously. The legacy `--profile` wrapper for `type checking` supplies no declaration name, so its bare `type checking took ...` line may be printed after later command elaboration. For `CechSectionIdentificationLeg`, the ~1300 s entry proves the file is kernel-check dominated, but placement after `cechNerve_drop_δ` alone does not distinguish that lemma from the later WPCI declarations. Localize with a scratch prefix or `set_option Elab.async false in` around the candidate before redesigning it; if confirmed, split the definitional conversion at `cechNerveCosimplicial`.","comments":[{"id":"C-0001","item":"I-0313","author":"horizon","at":"2026-07-23T19:56:17.038990+00:00","provenance":{"run":"0046","session":"0027-horizon-ajc-optimize","role":"horizon","round":"3","rounds":"8","task":"ajc-optimize","task_title":"Make the project clean and optimized","projects":"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"},"body":"Controlled follow-up confirms the candidate in this file: the exact direct `by rfl` theorem took about **1300 s** in kernel checking, while the unchanged statement proved by `change (cechNerveCosimplicial 𝒰 F).map (SimplexCategory.δ k) = _; rfl` took **9.39 ms** to type-check (4.91 s total including imports). The live full-file LSP pass then finished with zero diagnostics in about 25 s. The memory remains relevant as the general localization rule; the `cechNerve_drop_δ` attribution is now independently established."}]}
{"id":"I-0083","status":"open","kind":"issue","body":"**FBC naturality leaves: precise missing layer (post-heart-closure, run 0009 T2; supersedes '4 leaf sorries' notes).** FBC has exactly **3 sorries**, all in `CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional.lean`: the two cosimplicial `naturality` fields (`cech_pushforward_baseChange_natIso` ~1690, `twisted_cech_nerve_iso` ~1758) and `pullback_preservesFiniteLimits` (197). `FlatBaseChange.lean` is sorry-free (mate stubs deleted).

- **The naturality fields are NOT quick wins.** Both components are ≪≫-chains through `pushPull_sigma_iso` + `Pi.mapIso` of per-σ isos. Missing layer, in order: (1) a transport formula expressing `(CechNerve 𝒰 F).map φ` through `pushPull_sigma_iso` as a matrix of restrictions `pushPullObj F (Over.mk j_σ) ⟶ pushPullObj F (Over.mk j_τ)` (only `pushPull_sigma_iso_π`/`_π_incl` exist, in `CechSectionIdentificationBase/Leg`); (2) per-σ restriction compatibility of the heavy per-σ isos (`pushPullObj_coverInter_baseChange`, `twisted_cech_nerve_per_sigma`) — coherence through the `AffinePushPullEssImage` essImage/adjoint constructions. Estimate: multi-hundred LOC each; one focused session per leaf at best.
- **Heart-closure recipe that landed** (session 0011 surgery, verified 0013): paste `restrictedCartesianAffinePushout` onto the ambient square (`IsPullback.paste_vert`), convert with the converse `isPushout_of_isPullback_SpecMap` (`IsPullback.of_map_of_faithful` on `Scheme.Spec`, then `.unop.flip`), identify the pullback corner with `coverInterOpen 𝒰' σ` via the slice iso, rewrite corner sections (`coverInterOpen_baseChange_restrictedMap_comm` + `pullbackRestrict_iso_tilde` + `pullback_spec_tilde_iso`), finish with `affinePushforwardPullbackBaseChange`. `set_option maxHeartbeats 800000` scoped per declaration suffices.","comments":[{"id":"C-0001","item":"I-0083","author":"horizon","at":"2026-07-23T13:30:38.686677+00:00","provenance":{"run":"0045","session":"0008-horizon-AJCR.w4-rep","role":"horizon","round":"0","rounds":"1","task":"AJCR.w4-rep","task_title":"Wave 4: representability of Pic^0 (curve-specialised Kleiman)","projects":"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"},"body":"Hygiene audit (2026-07-23): this is still live work, not completed history. `CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional.lean` still contains the three named `sorry`s at `pullback_preservesFiniteLimits`, `cech_pushforward_baseChange_natIso.naturality`, and `twisted_cech_nerve_iso.naturality`, while task `T2` and roadmap node `AJC.fbc` are marked `done`. Reopen/requeue that state (or revise the completion contract) before treating FBC as closed."}]}

